{"base_rate":0.32063074901445465,"brier":0.14143298291721418,"bss":0.35070860814281646,"bss_hi":0.42559082530117226,"bss_lo":0.258005167276906,"country":"AT","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.08342969776609724,"ess":482.98045436682844,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Vienna</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Vienna rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 2 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (96%), believe about\n<b>80%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>7%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 761 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nWIEN, 3.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.35, ranked 47 of\n109 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(28&ndash;75) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>7%</b></td><td class='num'>298</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>14%</td><td class='num'><b>19%</b></td><td class='num'>90</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>38%</td><td class='num'><b>43%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>67%</td><td class='num'><b>59%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>96%</td><td class='num'><b>80%</b></td><td class='num'>153</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">2 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Vienna</b> <span class=\"muted\">AT</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">2 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.35</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>28&ndash;75\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 109</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>761 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Vienna &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Vienna\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.0,382.0 70.73343283582089,349.4029850746269 107.87466666666667,305.15555555555557 193.11766233766232,202.36363636363637 294.4813157894737,104.21052631578948 398.58039215686273,22.758169934640478 398.58039215686273,44.169934640522854 294.4813157894737,176.05263157894737 193.11766233766232,282.72727272727275 107.87466666666667,353.68888888888887 70.73343283582089,382.0 58.0,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"265.2904073587385\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"265.2904073587385\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0,356.3489932885906 70.73343283582089,349.4029850746269 107.87466666666667,313.2444444444444 193.11766233766232,226.0 294.4813157894737,166.47368421052633 398.58039215686273,91.75163398692808\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 7% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 298 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0\" cy=\"356.3489932885906\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 4%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"70.73343283582089\" cy=\"349.4029850746269\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 14%&amp;#10;It rained 19% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 90 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"107.87466666666667\" cy=\"313.2444444444444\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 38%&amp;#10;It rained 43% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"193.11766233766232\" cy=\"226.0\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 67%&amp;#10;It rained 59% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"294.4813157894737\" cy=\"166.47368421052633\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 96%&amp;#10;It rained 80% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 153 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"398.58039215686273\" cy=\"91.75163398692808\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(32%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Vienna the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.47) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.29).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>0.291</td><td class='num'>8.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'>0.301</td><td class='num'>11.2%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'>0.315</td><td class='num'>11.8%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>217</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>0.467</td><td class='num'>7.2%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":48.20849,"lon":16.37208,"n":761,"n_cities":109,"name":"Vienna","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.03,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0,"n":298,"obs":0.07046979865771812,"sig":true},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.03,"mean":0.03597014925373134,"n":67,"obs":0.08955223880597014,"sig":false},{"hi":0.25,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.1408888888888889,"n":90,"obs":0.18888888888888888,"sig":false},{"hi":0.53,"lo":0.25,"mean":0.3816883116883117,"n":77,"obs":0.42857142857142855,"sig":false},{"hi":0.83,"lo":0.53,"mean":0.6680263157894738,"n":76,"obs":0.5921052631578947,"sig":false},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.83,"mean":0.9620915032679738,"n":153,"obs":0.7973856209150327,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":3.2,"rank":47,"rank_hi":75.02499999999998,"rank_lo":28.0,"reliability":0.00872205812645334,"resolution":0.0854967507133094